valence relation since it's reflexive, symmetric, and transitive.\n\n- Relation III is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive because $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\notin N.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421407 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152066 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b70dd396-b01a-51e6-a52c-8ff729f48c45" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Standard Relation Is an Equivalence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40ad0690-c719-5974-8313-77c0307bc677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421327} {:answer/id #uuid "abdec431-c30d-53c6-9e45-5153802a2e1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40ad0690-c719-5974-8313-77c0307bc677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421327} :answer-field/id #uuid "99b2d851-fde5-5dcf-9ccf-b3176701b14b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421394} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4831cbaa-092f-5874-8d05-f8dd7f5fc544" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421328} {:answer/id #uuid "dc2c5cb7-d753-558a-afb1-296e3416064b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc2c5cb7-d753-558a-afb1-296e3416064b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421377} :answer-field/id #uuid "a15825e7-fb6f-53d4-8633-b3346886729b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421395} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53ec7024-bfbe-5876-a595-0e386cea622d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421335} {:answer/id #uuid "5e7b0772-5bcf-5f72-938e-f489bf04be5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e7b0772-5bcf-5f72-938e-f489bf04be5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421340} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba60e583-f0bb-5d89-9542-b0ca43b9fa37" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421397} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36eba4b6-28b6-571d-8217-a141e1dbf8be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421323} {:answer/id #uuid "5357d66d-1feb-5125-b851-a1faf4d4e579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5357d66d-1feb-5125-b851-a1faf4d4e579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421334} :answer-field/id #uuid "d01c36ca-21c0-59a4-b5b4-403ce3adfc4e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421399}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ce6b951-f687-5e96-9bbc-0957d6d3d0b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-214250" :question/problem "Consider the relation $y∣x$ defined on the set $Z.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n| The relation is reflexive | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- |\n| The relation is symmetric | {{field-2}} |\n| The relation is transitive | {{field-3}} |\n| The relation is an equivalence relation | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- It's $\\text{true}$ that the relation is reflexive. For all $x\\in Z,$ $x∣x.$\n\n- It's $\\text{false}$ that the relation is symmetric. For example, $1∣2$ but $2∤1.$\n\n- It's $\\text{true}$ that the relation is transitive. For all $x,y,z\\in Z,$ if $y∣x$ and $z∣y,$ then $z∣x.$\n\n- It's $\\text{false}$ that this is an equivalence relation since it's not symmetric."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152066 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b70dd396-b01a-51e6-a52c-8ff729f48c45" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Standard Relation Is an Equivalence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b40b244-4bab-58ee-bc64-fa1d33519579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, III, and IV" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421317} {:answer/id #uuid "52627dc2-eb63-52a8-8d5f-f961978b8947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421332} {:answer/id #uuid "5c380eff-8271-5e3c-a697-38aee4ec4cfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421338} {:answer/id #uuid "7560d387-5026-5568-9eb3-53e8af6d9cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421350} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a23ef4-cc98-56f0-ac39-ae3829545ef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52627dc2-eb63-52a8-8d5f-f961978b8947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421332} :answer-field/id #uuid "2eb12818-1e53-50fb-9686-e8410139c5cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72fa77bc-6d37-516a-bc08-8cef3db1618e" :question/math-academy-id "q-214252" :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $N.$\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,y∤x\n$$\n\n Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $R$ is reflexive\n- $R$ is symmetric\n- $R$ is transitive\n- $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is not reflexive. For example, $3∣3.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not symmetric. For example, $9∤3$ but $3∣9.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not transitive. For example, $3∤2$ and $2∤9,$ but $3∣9.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not an equivalence relation since it's neither reflexive nor symmetric nor transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421416 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152066 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b70dd396-b01a-51e6-a52c-8ff729f48c45" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Standard Relation Is an Equivalence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f1f7ce2-0886-55f8-8379-31f971e676b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421330} {:answer/id #uuid "6bbdf36e-3db7-54e8-862b-eb55ec298601" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f1f7ce2-0886-55f8-8379-31f971e676b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421330} :answer-field/id #uuid "228f10c0-5a8b-5fba-8458-2bce2af4a6eb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421386} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e50dec7-66a1-5309-b4d1-3ca325976f1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421339} {:answer/id #uuid "dc973c25-992c-5955-9151-75893641787b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e50dec7-66a1-5309-b4d1-3ca325976f1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421339} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ee9e05d-a1ec-5917-8ee3-429077480b99" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421392} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08f09ac8-e439-549e-86d5-86b2f7775049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421316} {:answer/id #uuid "57a76793-8553-5922-b416-bfc67112d95c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08f09ac8-e439-549e-86d5-86b2f7775049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421316} :answer-field/id #uuid "95f9516a-04fa-5063-891b-2622ee6802d7" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421393} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8956f580-15e2-5ec6-b015-fe8e0db5e2ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421352} {:answer/id #uuid "c728c867-0a42-5f45-871c-e98f82f70f08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8956f580-15e2-5ec6-b015-fe8e0db5e2ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421352} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2367340-22dc-5a13-9be5-b192f0b188dc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421398}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bb9f71b9-54fb-5914-9956-fcba4d5311e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-214254" :question/problem "Consider the relation $X⊆Y$ defined on the set $P(Q).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n| The relation is reflexive | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- |\n| The relation is symmetric | {{field-2}} |\n| The relation  is transitive | {{field-3}} |\n| The relation is an equivalence relation | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- It's $\\text{true}$ that the relation is reflexive. For all $X\\in P(Q),$ $X\\,⊆\\,X.$\n\n- It's $\\text{false}$ that the relation is symmetric. For example, $N⊆Z$ but $Z⊈N.$\n\n- It's $\\text{true}$ that the relation is transitive. For all $X,Y,Z\\in P(Q),$ if $X⊆Y$ and $Y⊆Z,$ then $X⊆Z.$\n\n- It's $\\text{false}$ that this is an equivalence relation since it's not symmetric."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421406 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152066 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b70dd396-b01a-51e6-a52c-8ff729f48c45" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Standard Relation Is an Equivalence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39fee494-92f8-5270-a473-d2107e7e8874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421324} {:answer/id #uuid "3fa9caf0-df86-5322-b028-e17f40231f57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, III, and IV" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421326} {:answer/id #uuid "6f67c691-2dcd-52d8-87bc-d5e99dedc4c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421347} {:answer/id #uuid "a05287c6-dfca-5030-894f-a2656886976e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421359} {:answer/id #uuid "bffd83c6-f97d-535a-871d-3201a645b707" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fa9caf0-df86-5322-b028-e17f40231f57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, III, and IV" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421326} :answer-field/id #uuid "52a03d34-71d7-5d2a-9d61-7aebbc62d675" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b086cc6-e229-5377-bb89-5a8ff879bb27" :question/math-academy-id "q-214271" :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $P(A),$ where $A={1,2,3,…,10}.$ \n\n$$\nX\\,R\\,Y\\,⇔\\,|X|=|Y|\n$$\n\n Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $R$ is reflexive\n- $R$ is symmetric\n- $R$ is transitive\n- $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive. For all $X\\in P(A),$ $|X|\\,=\\,|X|.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric. For all $X,Y\\in P(A),$ if $|X|\\,=\\,|Y|,$ then $|Y|=|X|.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive. For all $X,Y,Z\\in P(A),$ if $|X|=|Y|$ and $|Y|=|Z|,$ then $|X|=|Z|.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is an equivalence relation since it's reflexive, symmetric, and transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, III, and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421412 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "968df6ec-e87e-5770-9c11-e7c8d8a27e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations on Finite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0327b892-d3d1-5fb3-b2f0-3b4c1f296dde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421314} {:answer/id #uuid "3aa8f00c-f005-593e-8e78-a866a0839afc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421325} {:answer/id #uuid "6ff811d1-d506-5b23-8e83-bc217090e57c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421348} {:answer/id #uuid "9161f808-0aca-580f-99a3-789451a1123e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, III, and IV" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421356} {:answer/id #uuid "9dfb0cac-6b03-5126-9a12-63bea663b5bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dfb0cac-6b03-5126-9a12-63bea663b5bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421358} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2bbacab-cf91-5eed-be7e-c39a7e7d8711" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421401}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "73719e8c-e17e-53b6-804a-0ade3bbbaa7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-214273" :question/problem "Consider the relation $R$ on the set $A={a,b,c}$ defined as \n\n$$\nR={(a,a),(b,b),(c,c),(a,b),(b,a),(b,c),(c,b)}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $R$ is reflexive\n- $R$ is symmetric\n- $R$ is transitive\n- $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive because $(a,a),\\,(b,b),\\,(c,c)\\in R.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric because $(y,x)\\in R$ whenever $(x,y)\\in R.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is *not* transitive because $(a,b)\\in R$ and $(b,c)\\in R,$ but $(a,c)\\notin R$\n\n- The relation is *not* an equivalence relation since it's not transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421410 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "968df6ec-e87e-5770-9c11-e7c8d8a27e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations on Finite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2945124f-634b-58b9-9263-8fb5d84a8223" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421322} {:answer/id #uuid "529bac0f-0ab2-5dd2-829d-897c7a169213" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421333} {:answer/id #uuid "71db4ad8-a7c1-5de6-a688-cac7a9af590c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421349} {:answer/id #uuid "b2d02066-46a0-505f-9c99-5c4bf970eed7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421363} {:answer/id #uuid "e584f397-eac7-55f4-9aac-875dd305d2ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, III, and IV" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2945124f-634b-58b9-9263-8fb5d84a8223" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421322} :answer-field/id #uuid "e39d6c66-19f1-5b1f-bd77-f03b05414e51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72d1402f-e4b5-5dff-b1dc-9142e68fa197" :question/math-academy-id "q-214274" :question/problem "Consider the relation $R$ on the set $A={\\alpha ,\\beta ,\\gamma }$ defined as \n\n$$\nR={(\\alpha ,\\alpha ),(\\beta ,\\beta ),(\\beta ,\\alpha ),(\\alpha ,\\beta )}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $R$ is reflexive\n- $R$ is symmetric\n- $R$ is transitive\n- $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is *not* reflexive because $(\\gamma ,\\gamma )\\notin R.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric because $(y,x)\\in R$ whenever $(x,y)\\in R.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive because for all $x,y,z\\in {\\alpha ,\\beta ,\\gamma },$ if $(x,y)\\in R$ and $(y,z)\\in R,$ then $(x,z)\\in R.$ Recall that it's sufficient to check only the cases when both pairs have different components: \n\n- $(\\alpha ,\\beta )\\in R$ and $(\\beta ,\\alpha )\\in R,$ and also $(\\alpha ,\\alpha )\\in R$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $(\\beta ,\\alpha )\\in R$ and $(\\alpha ,\\beta )\\in R,$ and also $(\\beta ,\\beta )\\in R$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation is *not* an equivalence relation since it's not reflexive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421409 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "968df6ec-e87e-5770-9c11-e7c8d8a27e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations on Finite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6549b369-142b-53da-b553-4facda5dbfe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421342} {:answer/id #uuid "b40d20c9-3655-52ec-b8aa-91f39c99b226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, III, and IV" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421364} {:answer/id #uuid "b81f025c-684f-5d52-9d18-235fa3336997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421367} {:answer/id #uuid "c3273c40-cfce-55eb-8615-3692dd6d5895" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421369} {:answer/id #uuid "ce88d57b-0226-5ecc-89db-39d37dd6f50e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b40d20c9-3655-52ec-b8aa-91f39c99b226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, III, and IV" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421364} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa93e163-1d01-58a1-bdb6-eb95656804a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6ee391cd-217d-5ff1-a899-24ea6980b5eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-214279" :question/problem "Consider the relation $R$ on the set $A={∗,⋆,∘,⋄}$ defined as \n\n$$\nR={(∗,∗),(⋆,⋆),(∘,∘),(⋄,⋄),(∗,⋆),(⋆,∗)}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $R$ is reflexive\n- $R$ is symmetric\n- $R$ is transitive\n- $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive because $(∗,∗),(⋆,⋆),(∘,∘),(⋄,⋄)\\in R.$$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric because $(y,x)\\in R$ whenever $(x,y)\\in R.$$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive because for all $x,y,z\\in {∗,⋆,∘,⋄},$ if  $(x,y)\\in R$ and $(y,z)\\in R,$  then $(x,z)\\in R.$ Recall that it's sufficient to check only the cases when both pairs have different components: \n\n- $(∗,⋆)\\in R$ and $(⋆,∗)\\in R,$ and also $(∗,∗)\\in R$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $(⋆,∗)\\in R$ and $(∗,⋆)\\in R,$ and also $(⋆,⋆)\\in R$$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Since $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, it is an equivalence relation.$\\,\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, III, and IV.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421415 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "968df6ec-e87e-5770-9c11-e7c8d8