relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive because $(\\alpha ,\\alpha ),(\\beta ,\\beta )\\in R.$$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is *not* symmetric because $(\\alpha ,\\beta )\\in R$ but $(\\beta ,\\alpha )\\notin R.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive because it contains no \"linked\" pairs such that $(x,y)\\in R$ and $(y,z)\\in R.\\,✓$\n\n- The relation is *not* an equivalence relation since it's not symmetric.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421405 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152068 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7f9502e-19c3-58bb-98da-1562e0b0dfd0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "589ce36f-fb09-55ca-ab3b-7f3aa6166186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421337} {:answer/id #uuid "661dd547-fab0-5221-9f01-e96464c7b3af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421343} {:answer/id #uuid "a186ab13-4673-549f-8754-6fcd73c7e651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421360} {:answer/id #uuid "cf8cf821-8c18-5dd6-be5b-f58b8b837325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421374} {:answer/id #uuid "d79a90aa-2e9b-5f04-b081-64d7cc3f75e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a186ab13-4673-549f-8754-6fcd73c7e651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421360} :answer-field/id #uuid "da731a85-b255-5017-87f3-60d7f37421d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1a65003f-5b78-57dd-8ad6-282231fb787b" :question/math-academy-id "q-76164" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are equivalence relations on $R?$\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if $xy>0$\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if $x=2y$\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if $x-y$ is a rational number" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's consider each of the given relations.\n\n- Relation I is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive because $0\\cdot 0=0≯0.$\n\n- Relation II is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not symmetric because $2=2(1)$ but $1\\ne 2(2).$\n\n- Relation III is an equivalence relation:\n\n- It is reflexive because for all $x\\in R,$ we have $x-x=0$ is a rational number.\n\n- It is symmetric because for all $x,y\\in R,$ if $x-y=r$ is a rational number, then $y-x=-(x-y)=-r$ is also a rational number.\n\n- It is transitive because for all $x,y,z\\in R,$ if $x-y=r$ and $y-z=q,$ where $r,q$ are rational numbers, then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-z=(x-y)+(y-z)=r+q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis also a rational number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}]}
